@startuml Observability and Audit Flow - Clubinho NIB API
!theme plain
hide footbox
title Observability — request and job capture

actor Caller
participant RequestContextMiddleware as Context
participant "Controller / JobRunner" as Execution
participant "AuditInterceptor / ExceptionFilter" as Audit
participant StructuredLoggerService as Logs
queue LogDeliveryQueue as Queue
participant LogStorageProvider as Storage
database "AWS DynamoDB\nproduction logs" as DynamoDB
collections "JSONL files\nlocal development" as Files

Caller -> Context : HTTP request
Context -> Context : generate X-Request-Id
Context -> Execution : continue with request context

alt Successful mutation
  Execution -> Audit : record succeeded action once
else Rejected or failed request
  Execution -> Audit : record denied/rejected/not_found/failed once
  Execution -> Logs : technical warning or error
end

Audit -> Audit : noise filter\n(skip successful heartbeat, token refresh,\nnotification read)
Audit -> Queue : enqueue audit record\n(actor id, role and display name)
Logs -> Logs : noise filter\n(skip 401 and unmatched 404,\nskip filter echo of an error already recorded)
Logs -> Logs : repeat window (60 s)\nfirst record now, repeats counted
Logs -> Queue : enqueue observability record\n(error/fatal, 4xx as warn, repeat summary)
Queue -> Storage : sequential best-effort delivery
alt Configured storage is DynamoDB
  Storage -> DynamoDB : PutItem / UpdateItem
else Configured storage is file
  Storage -> Files : append protected JSONL record
end
Storage --> Queue : stored or failed

note over Queue, Storage
  Queue timeout/retry/failure never blocks the request.
  Sensitive request and personal data are not persisted,
  except the actor display name in audit records.
end note
@enduml
